Share on X Share on LinkedIn Print Share via Text Message Toronto Police. Kenneth Armstrong/TorontoToday Listen to this article 00:00:56 Two men were injured in a downtown stabbing early Friday morning, Toronto police reported.&nbsp; The incident occurred in the King Street West and Portland Street area around 4:35 a.m.&nbsp; Officers were called to the scene over reports of a stabbing. Upon arrival, they discovered two men with stab wounds.&nbsp; Both men were transported to hospital. Toronto Paramedic Services said the victims suffered serious, life-threatening injuries.&nbsp; Police have not yet released any information about a potential suspect.&nbsp; The investigation is ongoing.&nbsp; King Street West is currently closed from&nbsp;Portland&nbsp;to Brant streets as first responders remain at the scene.&nbsp;Southbound lanes of Portland Avenue are also closed at King Street West.&nbsp; Drivers in the area have been encouraged by police to use alternative routes.&nbsp; Trending Your vote matters This has been shared 0 times 0 Shares Share on SPACES Share by Email Share on Facebook Share on X Share on LinkedIn Print Share via Text Message Local News All Local News Arts &amp; Culture Business &amp; Economy City Planning &amp; Development Community Events Crime &amp; Emergency Services Education Environment &amp; Climate Family Food &amp; Dining Health History Lifestyle Opinion Policy Politics &amp; Government Real Estate &amp; Housing Science &amp; Technology Sports Transportation &amp; Infrastructure More News Neighbourhoods Bloordale Cabbagetown Church-Wellesley Village Distillery District Downtown Core Dufferin Grove Entertainment District Garden District-TMU Harbord Village Kensington Market-Chinatown Liberty Village Little Italy Moss Park Old Town Riverdale-Danforth Riverside-Leslieville Roncesvalles-Parkdale Seaton Village-Christie Pits The Annex The Junction Waterfront and the Islands West Queen West Yorkville City Hall More News Games and Comics Ontario New